WEBVTT

00:06.840 --> 00:08.007
Arisu!

00:15.098 --> 00:16.391
Arisu!

00:26.901 --> 00:28.319
Arisu!

01:35.428 --> 01:36.346
Aguni…

01:39.224 --> 01:41.476
Yo, newbie.

01:43.812 --> 01:45.146
So, you survived.

01:47.232 --> 01:48.399
As luck would have it.

01:50.777 --> 01:52.028
I ran into Niragi too.

01:55.073 --> 01:56.741
Guess he cheated death too.

02:02.205 --> 02:03.623
What about your other pals?

02:06.668 --> 02:08.419
We got separated from Ann and Chishiya.

02:10.380 --> 02:12.215
Kuina went to look for them.

02:14.801 --> 02:16.302
Tatta died in a game.

02:19.347 --> 02:22.433
I'm going to look for Usagi now.

02:24.727 --> 02:25.645
I see.

02:29.107 --> 02:30.275
Where are you going?

02:31.568 --> 02:33.403
To kill the King of Spades.

02:33.486 --> 02:34.779
Give us a hand.

02:35.488 --> 02:36.865
How are you going to kill him?

02:37.657 --> 02:39.325
He's still just a human.

02:40.118 --> 02:41.786
He'll have weaknesses.

02:43.204 --> 02:44.497
You'll never kill that guy.

02:46.332 --> 02:49.711
Yeah, so he's the perfect opponent for me.

02:50.920 --> 02:53.798
It's the perfect game
for someone looking for a place to die.

02:54.591 --> 02:55.884
"A place to die"?

02:55.967 --> 02:58.177
I cheated death at the Beach.

02:59.804 --> 03:03.391
I don't have anywhere to go back to
or look forward to.

03:08.062 --> 03:09.480
Don't get me involved in this.

03:16.988 --> 03:18.990
I've always wanted to ask you this.

03:20.575 --> 03:21.993
What are you living for?

03:23.745 --> 03:25.622
What is your purpose for living?

03:27.332 --> 03:28.875
To get back to your life before?

03:29.459 --> 03:31.544
Or to get a taste
of that chick you're after?

03:33.212 --> 03:34.213
Aguni…

03:37.133 --> 03:39.385
I don't need a reason to live.

03:44.766 --> 03:46.517
As long as I'm still alive here,

03:48.978 --> 03:50.063
I want to keep living.

03:53.816 --> 03:55.318
Even if I've lost my purpose.

03:59.280 --> 04:00.698
Such a weak spirit.

04:02.992 --> 04:04.577
But that's what we humans are.

04:07.288 --> 04:08.122
Yeah.

04:09.791 --> 04:10.959
I'm jealous.

04:39.445 --> 04:42.156
Whoa! No way! Your nails are so cute!

04:42.240 --> 04:44.492
- Yeah! Aren't they?
- Where'd you get them done?

04:44.575 --> 04:48.288
Let me see… A place near the station.
I forgot the name.

04:48.371 --> 04:49.831
- Behind us.
- Hey, you guys!

04:51.708 --> 04:54.294
- Want to go barbecue with us next Sunday?
- Barbecue!

04:54.377 --> 04:55.378
A barbecue?

04:55.461 --> 04:57.422
- Yeah.
- We'll cook out together.

04:57.505 --> 05:00.300
To remember
our last summer in high school,

05:00.383 --> 05:02.719
- let's go camping by the river!
- Sorry.

05:02.802 --> 05:05.138
That day's the anniversary
of my mom's death.

05:05.638 --> 05:07.098
Oh… Sorry.

05:07.598 --> 05:09.726
We didn't know that. Sorry.

05:11.769 --> 05:13.771
Of course, you didn't. I never told you.

05:13.855 --> 05:15.231
What would I say?

05:15.315 --> 05:18.151
"That dumb bitch died on a trip
when she was having an affair"?

05:19.527 --> 05:21.029
Besides, it's so fucking hot,

05:21.112 --> 05:23.698
so why would we want
to go barbecue outside with you guys?

05:23.781 --> 05:27.660
- Heiya, that's going a bit far.
- They clearly have ulterior motives.

05:28.244 --> 05:30.997
Did you think you had a chance with us?
Stupid fucks!

05:31.080 --> 05:33.666
- For sure.
- Now, now. You'll hurt their feelings.

05:33.750 --> 05:34.917
You think?

05:35.001 --> 05:36.711
Later!

05:39.422 --> 05:41.507
Wait. Don't you have
archery practice today?

05:42.008 --> 05:43.885
I've lost interest lately.

05:43.968 --> 05:47.180
You know, I heard Megu
and her boyfriend are gonna break up.

05:47.263 --> 05:49.098
Seriously? With Odaken?

05:49.807 --> 05:51.434
- They used to be so close.
- Yeah.

05:52.435 --> 05:53.853
Actually, they weren't.

05:55.646 --> 05:58.357
- What? What do you mean?
- How would you know?

05:59.484 --> 06:01.527
He said he was sick of her.

06:01.611 --> 06:03.863
He said he prefers me over Megu.

06:03.946 --> 06:04.822
What?

06:05.406 --> 06:07.283
Wait! You mean you hooked up with Odaken?

06:07.784 --> 06:09.994
He's the one who asked me.

06:10.078 --> 06:11.996
- No way!
- Only because you enticed him.

06:12.663 --> 06:16.834
You really will do whatever it takes
to get the man you want.

06:18.336 --> 06:21.047
- There's that look!
- Oh, cut that…

06:56.958 --> 06:59.544
PLAYERS, PLEASE GATHER
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE FIELD

07:00.128 --> 07:04.507
1 PER PERSON

07:37.165 --> 07:38.624
PLEASE WAIT UNTIL THE GAME BEGINS.
THERE ARE CURRENTLY 17 PARTICIPANTS.

07:38.708 --> 07:39.709
"Game"?

07:40.710 --> 07:41.711
What's this all about?

07:44.380 --> 07:45.798
What the heck is this?

07:47.467 --> 07:49.051
Where'd everyone go?

07:51.679 --> 07:53.264
If you want to survive,

07:54.891 --> 07:57.059
you've got to clear the game.

08:02.523 --> 08:04.734
Difficulty, Seven of Spades.

08:05.735 --> 08:07.403
Game, "Boiling Death."

08:08.779 --> 08:13.534
Rules: If you escape the arena
before it collapses,

08:13.618 --> 08:14.785
you clear the game.

08:20.958 --> 08:22.460
What the hell is this?

08:34.263 --> 08:35.806
Oh, shit. What is this?

08:41.812 --> 08:45.149
No way! I'm out of here!

08:45.733 --> 08:46.984
Forget this!

10:15.990 --> 10:18.409
It's hot! Oh god, it's hot!

10:29.795 --> 10:30.963
I've got to pull it out.

11:53.462 --> 11:54.380
Okay.

12:13.691 --> 12:17.528
I'll admit, I was a pretty shitty person!

12:18.571 --> 12:22.700
So I understand that
getting sent here was meant to punish me!

12:25.327 --> 12:27.538
But why do I have to go through this shit?

12:30.291 --> 12:32.084
It's all that bitch's fault!

12:59.653 --> 13:01.322
This is so unlike you.

13:09.955 --> 13:11.040
Takeru.

13:27.431 --> 13:28.599
Why…

13:30.476 --> 13:32.728
are you with those guys?

13:37.358 --> 13:39.068
You even rescued Arisu.

13:40.819 --> 13:43.155
Are you trying to atone

13:44.365 --> 13:48.702
for killing all those people
in your attempt to die with the Beach?

13:51.121 --> 13:55.501
Going down in a blaze of glory
fighting the King of Spades…

13:57.169 --> 13:59.588
is more than one
who cheated death deserves.

14:07.304 --> 14:09.306
If you want to die so badly,

14:12.017 --> 14:14.019
why don't you just kill yourself?

14:33.372 --> 14:34.540
Aguni.

14:35.708 --> 14:37.126
Let's just stop this.

14:38.586 --> 14:40.504
Don't let the deaths of the innocent…

14:41.797 --> 14:43.299
go to waste.

14:46.677 --> 14:47.845
I understand that.

14:49.346 --> 14:50.681
Go away.

15:33.265 --> 15:34.516
You awake?

15:42.316 --> 15:43.943
What? Are you a virgin?

15:44.026 --> 15:45.027
No!

15:59.166 --> 16:00.250
Okay…

16:01.460 --> 16:03.295
So, which way to the city?

16:03.963 --> 16:06.215
What? You're going already?

16:07.007 --> 16:08.175
I'm looking for someone.

16:10.135 --> 16:12.137
You mean that "Usagi" person?

16:12.846 --> 16:13.764
Is she a woman?

16:14.598 --> 16:15.849
Don't eavesdrop.

16:25.025 --> 16:26.694
Who's prettier, me or her?

16:27.277 --> 16:28.195
What?

16:31.699 --> 16:33.033
Must be me, right?

16:33.617 --> 16:34.660
No…

16:34.743 --> 16:36.203
What are you blushing for?

16:36.286 --> 16:37.371
I'm not blushing.

16:46.880 --> 16:48.632
I guess you're acceptable.

16:49.425 --> 16:50.259
What?

16:50.843 --> 16:54.096
- You're good enough. Let's do it.
- What? Hey!

16:55.264 --> 16:58.767
We live in a stressful world
and could die any second,

16:58.851 --> 17:00.352
so a woman has to cut loose.

17:00.436 --> 17:02.187
- Cut it out!
- You know you want it.

17:09.862 --> 17:12.781
This isn't what you think!
Don't get the wrong idea!

17:12.865 --> 17:16.452
I mean, you never pay me
any attention, Aguni.

17:16.535 --> 17:18.370
We're moving out. Get up.

17:19.788 --> 17:20.789
I'm not going with you.

17:21.290 --> 17:22.499
I'm going to look for Usagi.

17:23.083 --> 17:25.669
You need to worry more
about yourself instead of others.

17:26.795 --> 17:29.673
He only attacks
when he's got a pretty clear target.

17:30.299 --> 17:32.551
He might know where we are.

17:33.093 --> 17:34.094
I don't know how.

17:34.678 --> 17:36.764
But it's too dangerous
to stay in one place.

17:37.431 --> 17:39.600
We'll lure him into
a suitable spot in the hills

17:40.225 --> 17:41.226
and kill him.

17:43.145 --> 17:45.814
We need as many people as possible now.
Take this.

17:48.859 --> 17:49.735
Wait!

17:51.904 --> 17:54.239
Oh, god. He's such a stud.

17:59.536 --> 18:03.290
The King of Spades targets areas
with lots of people.

18:05.042 --> 18:07.878
But he seems to come after us a lot too.

18:07.961 --> 18:09.713
He probably targets
troublesome people too.

18:10.506 --> 18:12.591
I'll find a place we can lure him into.

18:18.972 --> 18:21.058
The King of Spades never stops killing.

18:22.351 --> 18:24.770
He's greatly reduced
the number of surviving players.

18:26.063 --> 18:29.108
We escaped to the forest outside
the city thinking it would be safe,

18:29.608 --> 18:31.068
but he still came after us.

18:35.197 --> 18:38.534
According to my compass,
we should be near Kichijoji Station.

18:39.743 --> 18:40.744
Then what's this place?

19:11.859 --> 19:14.027
He must've killed himself
before his visa ran out.

19:15.487 --> 19:18.991
What an idiotic way to die,
without even trying to fight.

19:20.200 --> 19:22.536
In this world,
I can understand why he did it.

19:25.080 --> 19:27.332
I'll never take my own life,
no matter what.

19:29.585 --> 19:31.795
Have you lost anyone
precious to you in these games?

19:34.798 --> 19:35.799
No.

19:38.510 --> 19:39.678
But I did lose…

19:41.805 --> 19:44.099
a part of my own precious self.

20:38.445 --> 20:39.446
Akane.

20:45.494 --> 20:46.495
Mom?

20:50.958 --> 20:52.542
What are you doing here?

21:03.929 --> 21:04.930
Akane!

21:17.526 --> 21:18.527
Come here.

21:28.370 --> 21:30.289
I can trust you, right?

22:02.529 --> 22:03.947
It's not hot here!

22:12.414 --> 22:15.083
I was the only one
who survived my first game.

22:17.711 --> 22:20.380
Who would've ever thought
the ghost of that stupid, cheating bitch

22:20.464 --> 22:22.299
would have saved me?

22:46.865 --> 22:48.617
It's turning a funny color.

22:51.661 --> 22:52.496
I'll die.

22:53.080 --> 22:54.331
I'll die at this rate!

22:56.958 --> 22:59.461
That's a pretty bad case
of gangrene there.

23:08.303 --> 23:12.224
Unless that foot is cut off, you'll die.

23:13.725 --> 23:14.726
Are you a doctor?

23:16.937 --> 23:17.938
Then help me!

23:18.814 --> 23:20.398
For free?

23:20.482 --> 23:23.110
You want money? How can I possibly pay?

23:24.736 --> 23:26.238
What? Money?

23:27.030 --> 23:29.866
That shit's useless in this world.

23:30.617 --> 23:31.868
You know what I want.

23:47.509 --> 23:48.802
Fine…

23:53.515 --> 23:55.433
Now hurry up
and do something with this foot!

24:16.580 --> 24:19.166
My future self owes me one.

24:20.917 --> 24:25.255
The only reason I'm here now
is that I worked so hard to survive then!

24:27.174 --> 24:29.426
So I swore that I'm never going to die.

24:31.344 --> 24:32.846
I'll survive no matter what.

26:08.400 --> 26:10.151
I looked too, but there's nothing.

26:22.664 --> 26:24.165
You can have these if you like.

26:33.508 --> 26:34.592
Thank you.

26:37.846 --> 26:38.847
Is he your son?

26:42.600 --> 26:45.520
I saw him all alone at a Game Arena.

26:47.605 --> 26:48.773
Where are your parents?

26:57.532 --> 26:59.200
I think they may be dead.

27:00.285 --> 27:02.454
He doesn't have much time left
on his visa either.

27:02.954 --> 27:04.914
I couldn't leave him on his own.

27:06.374 --> 27:07.292
Then…

27:08.668 --> 27:10.295
even if he makes it back,

27:12.255 --> 27:13.340
it'll be harsh for him.

27:16.926 --> 27:18.345
Yes, it probably will be.

27:21.473 --> 27:22.390
But…

27:23.516 --> 27:28.938
I'm sure his parents want him
to survive and return to the real world.

27:31.691 --> 27:34.027
They'll want him to find happiness there.

27:35.737 --> 27:36.738
I'm sure of it.

28:00.512 --> 28:01.471
Yuzuha.

28:02.347 --> 28:03.348
Yeah?

28:03.973 --> 28:05.975
If I die in a climbing accident,

28:07.310 --> 28:09.062
don't you cry for me.

28:10.397 --> 28:11.398
What's that all about?

28:12.315 --> 28:16.403
For me, dying in the mountains
is what I want.

28:16.986 --> 28:18.154
Cut that out.

28:20.281 --> 28:25.537
Becoming an old man
and dying in a hospital isn't for me.

28:30.917 --> 28:32.293
If I do die in the mountains,

28:33.044 --> 28:35.380
it's proof that
I've lived life to the fullest.

28:37.382 --> 28:38.800
So even if that does happen,

28:39.467 --> 28:43.388
I want you to live your own life
to the fullest too, okay?

29:44.407 --> 29:47.160
I should be in Yokohama by now.

30:06.346 --> 30:08.765
How far does this forest continue?

31:02.485 --> 31:04.571
We'll lure him here.

31:05.572 --> 31:06.739
Here?

31:07.615 --> 31:08.700
It's a cliff!

31:09.492 --> 31:11.077
Nobody asked for your opinion.

31:20.253 --> 31:21.296
Flares?

31:21.379 --> 31:23.840
We'll set up a trap
so we know we're being attacked.

31:24.507 --> 31:26.384
And we can see the enemy even in the dark.

31:27.427 --> 31:29.637
It'd be better if we had grenades,

31:30.638 --> 31:32.140
but we can at least set up tripwires.

31:33.516 --> 31:34.517
Just tripwires?

31:35.268 --> 31:37.812
There's no need
for the whole trap to be real.

31:37.896 --> 31:41.107
What's important is to put stress
and pressure on the enemy.

31:42.650 --> 31:43.651
You sure know a lot.

31:44.235 --> 31:45.236
Yeah, I do.

31:45.320 --> 31:46.321
I taught her.

31:47.697 --> 31:49.198
You stand guard by the tent.

34:24.020 --> 34:25.271
I was the bait?

34:25.354 --> 34:27.023
You're a natural at being a decoy.

34:30.818 --> 34:31.903
Is that guy immortal?

34:32.487 --> 34:33.529
It's a bulletproof vest.

34:33.613 --> 34:35.031
He must be a mercenary.

34:35.865 --> 34:38.409
Let's cover each other
and force him over that cliff.

34:39.911 --> 34:40.787
Go!

35:26.707 --> 35:27.834
Arisu! Run!

35:35.258 --> 35:36.384
Arisu!

36:18.301 --> 36:19.218
Aguni?

38:39.650 --> 38:40.526
Usagi!

38:55.207 --> 38:56.208
Sorry.

40:02.400 --> 40:04.235
Yes!

40:05.027 --> 40:06.570
We won!

40:10.783 --> 40:12.785
Yeah!

40:17.790 --> 40:20.751
- We won!
- Yes! We did it!

40:21.877 --> 40:22.878
Usagi!

40:27.341 --> 40:28.342
Usagi!

40:49.280 --> 40:50.781
I've cheated death again.

41:04.503 --> 41:05.838
Go away.

41:12.011 --> 41:13.095
Go away!

41:17.725 --> 41:18.642
Aguni?

41:22.396 --> 41:23.981
You're awake?

41:29.862 --> 41:31.030
Thank god!

41:35.242 --> 41:37.411
Thank god!

42:54.572 --> 42:56.907
Difficulty level, Jack of Spades.

43:39.074 --> 43:40.826
These face card games are rough.

43:41.493 --> 43:43.162
Going at it alone is brutal.

43:45.873 --> 43:47.207
I'm covered in wounds.

44:15.986 --> 44:17.488
But I refuse to give up.

45:20.384 --> 45:21.718
What is this world?

45:55.002 --> 45:56.003
I won't go.

46:00.257 --> 46:01.341
Do you want to die?

46:05.637 --> 46:08.432
Then let's win and survive.

46:11.101 --> 46:12.436
What'll happen if we win?

46:18.233 --> 46:19.234
I'm sure…

46:20.986 --> 46:22.571
we'll return to the real world.

46:26.783 --> 46:28.118
My mom and dad…

46:30.496 --> 46:31.914
They're not there anymore.

46:37.085 --> 46:38.003
But…

46:39.505 --> 46:42.883
what do you think
your mom and dad would want you to do?

46:47.054 --> 46:48.597
They'd want me to go back.

46:51.225 --> 46:52.059
Then let's go.

47:41.024 --> 47:41.942
Hey, sweetie.

47:42.442 --> 47:43.860
How old are you?

47:44.987 --> 47:45.904
I'm ten.

47:48.031 --> 47:49.116
Good kid.

47:54.329 --> 47:56.790
This is a spade game.
You'll never win with a kid.

47:57.833 --> 48:00.419
I'll get rid of anyone
who holds us back, even a child.

48:02.212 --> 48:03.213
Don't hold it against me.

48:09.136 --> 48:10.387
But you'll win, Usagi.

48:17.269 --> 48:18.353
Arisu…

48:20.022 --> 48:21.023
Usagi.

48:28.530 --> 48:30.032
I knew you were still alive.

48:31.575 --> 48:32.576
Me too.

48:34.369 --> 48:35.954
How did you know I was here?

48:37.706 --> 48:39.374
You're good at physical games.

48:40.334 --> 48:43.837
Besides the King of Spades,
the only spade left is the Queen.

49:16.870 --> 49:17.788
This boy…

49:18.413 --> 49:20.707
His visa expires today.

49:21.333 --> 49:22.334
Is that right?

49:23.835 --> 49:27.089
I thought I could help him
if we played a spade game.

49:35.347 --> 49:37.516
Game, "Checkmate."

49:38.016 --> 49:39.101
"Checkmate"?

49:40.936 --> 49:46.775
The Queen Team will compete
against you, the Challenger Team.

49:47.984 --> 49:49.069
Welcome!

49:49.861 --> 49:53.031
This is the Game Arena of
beautiful physiques and vigorous activity.

49:53.824 --> 49:56.493
I am the Queen of Spades.

49:57.577 --> 50:01.248
There are four members
of the Queen Team, including me.

50:01.331 --> 50:04.167
There are 16 members of your team,
the Challenger Team.

50:04.960 --> 50:06.837
Are they citizens too?

50:07.421 --> 50:10.674
One person on each team
will be designated the King.

50:11.550 --> 50:13.218
The King of the Queen Team…

50:14.177 --> 50:15.345
is me.

50:16.763 --> 50:19.599
As for the Challenger Team…

50:20.934 --> 50:23.270
Who shall I pick?

50:25.397 --> 50:26.398
I know.

50:28.275 --> 50:29.526
I'll choose that boy.

50:47.377 --> 50:50.630
The rules will now be explained.

50:52.299 --> 50:56.303
Each team will alternate taking turns
for a total of 16 rounds.

50:56.928 --> 50:58.722
When it is the Queen Team's turn,

50:58.805 --> 51:03.393
the members of the Queen Team will chase
the members of the Challenger Team.

51:03.894 --> 51:08.064
When the button on your back is pressed,
the button's light changes

51:08.148 --> 51:10.776
from blue to red, the Queen Team's color.

51:10.859 --> 51:12.986
THE BUTTON COLOR CHANGES TO RED,
THE QUEEN TEAM'S COLOR.

51:13.069 --> 51:16.656
Also, during the rest of that round,
you can no longer move.

51:17.365 --> 51:18.992
From the next round,

51:19.075 --> 51:23.079
you must act
as a member of the Queen Team.

51:24.080 --> 51:28.293
However, the King cannot change teams.

51:29.753 --> 51:33.757
During the Challenger Team's turn,
the roles are reversed.

51:34.508 --> 51:37.010
Each round lasts for five minutes.

51:37.636 --> 51:40.222
The teams switch roles after each round.

51:40.305 --> 51:44.851
Then after 16 rounds, the team
with the most members is the victor.

51:45.352 --> 51:49.606
Everyone on the losing team,
including the King, dies.

51:51.024 --> 51:52.275
What does all that mean?

51:53.443 --> 51:54.653
I think

51:55.529 --> 51:57.364
it's like chess or shogi.

51:57.948 --> 52:00.075
If the other team
presses the button on our back,

52:00.158 --> 52:01.701
we go to the other team.

52:01.785 --> 52:05.789
Then, like in shogi, from the next turn,

52:05.872 --> 52:07.749
we fight like a member of the other team.

52:09.960 --> 52:12.295
Please equip yourselves with a button.

52:22.138 --> 52:23.306
We have to put this on?

52:32.649 --> 52:33.650
It turned on.

52:34.651 --> 52:38.113
Round 1, the Queen Team's turn,
will now commence.

52:38.697 --> 52:40.991
The round lasts for five minutes.

52:41.575 --> 52:42.951
The game will now start.

52:52.002 --> 52:53.211
Shit, they're coming!

52:55.589 --> 52:56.840
They're headed this way!

52:57.424 --> 53:00.385
If we stick together, they'll get us
all at once! Let's split up!

53:00.468 --> 53:02.137
- Right! Everyone, run!
- Okay!

53:02.220 --> 53:03.305
- Go!
- Right!

53:11.688 --> 53:12.606
Wait here.

53:13.189 --> 53:14.816
I swear we'll protect you.

53:16.359 --> 53:17.277
Okay.

53:17.360 --> 53:18.194
Let's go, Usagi.

53:30.665 --> 53:32.918
Go! Hurry up!

53:37.839 --> 53:40.091
Come on! Quickly, this way!

53:41.718 --> 53:43.386
- Run!
- Don't leave me!

54:12.624 --> 54:15.669
Once your button is pressed,
you can't move for the rest of the round.

54:16.169 --> 54:18.964
You'll fight for my team next round.

54:25.303 --> 54:26.805
Up there! They're above us!

54:29.057 --> 54:29.933
Where?

54:31.059 --> 54:32.644
They're heading your way!

55:04.968 --> 55:08.096
Round 1 will be ending soon.

55:08.805 --> 55:12.976
Ten, nine, eight, seven…

55:13.059 --> 55:15.645
- Damn. There are more red lights.
- six, five, four…

55:16.229 --> 55:18.106
- The Queen's turn will end soon.
- three, two,

55:18.189 --> 55:19.190
one.

55:20.775 --> 55:23.445
The Challenger Team's turn
will now commence.

55:25.030 --> 55:27.032
The round lasts for five minutes.

55:27.741 --> 55:28.742
Start.

55:29.576 --> 55:31.327
Let's get back the people they caught.

55:31.411 --> 55:34.414
There's no way
they'll actively work for the Queen.

55:34.497 --> 55:36.207
They'll try to get back
to our team for sure.

55:36.291 --> 55:38.251
You're right. Okay, let's go!

55:42.505 --> 55:44.632
Hey! Over here!

55:44.716 --> 55:45.925
Over here!

55:46.009 --> 55:48.762
Up here! I'm here!

55:48.845 --> 55:50.096
Come and help me!

55:50.680 --> 55:51.723
- I'm on my way!
- Okay.

55:52.223 --> 55:53.058
Don't move.

55:53.641 --> 55:54.559
Hurry!

56:01.858 --> 56:02.692
Hey!

56:03.735 --> 56:04.652
There he is!

56:05.862 --> 56:07.030
Here! Please!

56:20.293 --> 56:21.795
The Queen's attacking?

56:21.878 --> 56:23.171
She's using force.

56:24.005 --> 56:27.175
The rules didn't say anything
against using force.

56:29.219 --> 56:32.555
Round 3, the Queen Team's turn,
will now commence.

56:33.640 --> 56:35.642
The round lasts for five minutes.

56:36.309 --> 56:37.227
Start.

56:38.144 --> 56:41.731
Anyway, we'll have to split up
and get them back one by one.

56:41.815 --> 56:44.400
If we split up,
we won't know where each other is.

56:44.484 --> 56:45.568
We may never meet again!

56:51.950 --> 56:54.619
When a new round starts,
there's a siren and an announcement.

56:58.957 --> 57:02.502
Let's look out from the ocean side
and see where each other is at that point.

57:03.128 --> 57:03.962
Okay.

57:30.071 --> 57:30.905
No!

57:30.989 --> 57:33.241
Stay back! Back!

57:42.500 --> 57:43.960
Do you want to survive?

57:45.837 --> 57:46.754
Of course.

57:47.422 --> 57:49.507
Then join my team.

57:51.342 --> 57:53.845
One minute remaining in Round 5.

58:11.446 --> 58:12.530
Hold up! Dammit!

58:22.290 --> 58:23.458
Shit!

58:45.313 --> 58:46.147
Found you!

58:52.028 --> 58:53.613
Yes!

58:54.322 --> 58:55.240
Damn…

58:58.701 --> 59:02.539
Round 10, the Challenger Team's turn,
will now commence.

59:03.039 --> 59:04.791
The round lasts for five minutes.

59:05.375 --> 59:06.376
Start.

59:07.794 --> 59:08.795
I'll get you now!

59:14.259 --> 59:15.593
What? Hey, hold on!

59:31.609 --> 59:35.196
Round 11, the Queen Team's turn,
will now commence.

59:35.697 --> 59:37.532
The round lasts for five minutes.

59:38.116 --> 59:38.950
Start.

59:39.951 --> 59:41.619
- You okay?
- Yeah.

59:45.498 --> 59:47.584
- Hurry up!
- Go!

59:48.793 --> 59:50.211
- Wait!
- Why?

59:53.715 --> 59:55.717
- Hey wait!
- No!

01:00:13.568 --> 01:00:15.153
You stay on the Queen Team too.

01:00:16.321 --> 01:00:17.155
What?

01:00:19.657 --> 01:00:22.869
If we stay here, we don't have to
participate in other games.

01:00:23.494 --> 01:00:26.247
We won't be chased down
and shot by the King of Spades either.

01:00:27.415 --> 01:00:28.583
Nice, isn't it?

01:00:29.959 --> 01:00:33.129
Are you players too? Like us?

01:00:33.212 --> 01:00:34.130
That's right.

01:00:34.631 --> 01:00:37.634
We played this game last time
and joined the Queen Team.

01:00:38.551 --> 01:00:41.137
The Queen is tough. She'll always win.

01:00:41.638 --> 01:00:43.765
When we win, we can stay in this arena.

01:00:44.515 --> 01:00:48.019
As long as the Queen lives,
this game keeps on being played.

01:00:48.519 --> 01:00:49.520
In other words,

01:00:50.355 --> 01:00:53.691
as long as we're on the Queen Team,
we can survive.

01:00:55.026 --> 01:00:56.027
How about it?

01:00:56.694 --> 01:00:57.945
Awesome, isn't it?

01:01:19.008 --> 01:01:21.386
- Found him?
- No. I'll look up higher.

01:01:21.886 --> 01:01:23.388
- Okay!
- Damn!

01:01:30.520 --> 01:01:34.524
Instead of dying in some other game,
it's way better to stay here and survive.

01:01:38.152 --> 01:01:41.072
This game is easy
when we're all on the same team.

01:01:41.698 --> 01:01:43.950
Let's all work with the Queen!

01:01:51.958 --> 01:01:53.042
That boy…

01:01:54.085 --> 01:01:55.336
I feel sorry for him.

01:01:56.546 --> 01:01:57.380
Yeah.

01:01:58.423 --> 01:01:59.841
But it can't be helped.

01:02:02.009 --> 01:02:04.011
There are only three of them left.

01:02:06.097 --> 01:02:07.265
Victory is within our grasp.

01:02:08.933 --> 01:02:10.935
You people will survive.

01:02:13.229 --> 01:02:14.230
Oh, yeah.

01:02:14.313 --> 01:02:15.398
But…

01:02:16.524 --> 01:02:18.276
there's one more that I want.

01:02:19.110 --> 01:02:20.111
One more?

01:02:20.695 --> 01:02:23.197
The guy who was with
the woman who brought the kid.

01:02:24.198 --> 01:02:26.701
Oh, him. She called him "Arisu."

01:02:28.369 --> 01:02:29.787
That guy…

01:02:35.209 --> 01:02:36.294
He's my type.

01:02:39.714 --> 01:02:42.383
Two people remaining until checkmate.

01:02:42.884 --> 01:02:46.512
Round 13, the Queen Team's turn,
will now commence.

01:02:47.096 --> 01:02:48.848
The round lasts for five minutes.

01:02:49.557 --> 01:02:50.391
Start.

01:02:54.771 --> 01:02:55.688
Found him!

01:03:16.876 --> 01:03:17.710
Go!

01:03:17.794 --> 01:03:19.003
She's after you, Arisu!

01:03:19.879 --> 01:03:20.797
What?

01:06:06.379 --> 01:06:11.384
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
